# VDX Android — Cursor Rules

## Product bar (canonical)
- Spec: ~/vdx/docs/VDX_PRODUCT_SPEC.md — **V1 task matrix + better**, tap-to-talk speak/click, low vision primary
- Benchmark: the V1 task matrix (WhatsApp, Uber, YouTube, Gmail, Contacts/SMS/Calls, web, store, system, PDF/OCR)
- Interaction: user chooses when to speak (bubble tap) and when to click — NOT continuous beep-menus
- Audience: low vision who can read; completely blind screen-reader replacement is out of V1 scope

## Architecture
- Live path: BubbleForegroundService → VoiceCaptureManager (PCM) → SonicEngine → Planner (adapters) → com.vdx.sonic.robot.RobotHand
- Legacy path retained for MainActivity harness: VdxIntent → com.vdx.RobotHand
- App adapters must grow to full depth per package — “open app” alone is not done
- Long-press → diagnostics / keyboard fallback

## Spec docs
- ~/vdx/docs/VDX_PRODUCT_SPEC.md — canonical product brief
- ~/vdx/docs/vdx-sonic-architecture.md — 10-layer architecture
- ~/vdx/docs/v2-complete-plan.md — V2 memory graph
- ~/vdx/agentos/GOVERNANCE/ADRS/ — ADRs

## Coding rules
1. No reflection — use VdxAccessibilityService.instance / BubbleForegroundService.isRunning
2. No Thread.sleep() in suspend functions — use delay()
3. Bound tree traversal (max depth 5, max nodes 100)
4. Confirm destructive actions (send / book / call / delete)
5. Test before push: ./gradlew.bat testDebugUnitTest
6. Spec compliance = full depth for the domain, not shallow happy path

## Code review checklist
1. Dual-path execution (old vs Sonic)
2. Reflection-based service access
3. Thread.sleep() in coroutines
4. Unbounded accessibility tree traversal
5. Dead code / unused paths
6. V1 capability for the touched app domain
7. speak-or-tap preserved (no forced continuous dialogue)
